// Ngân hàng câu hỏi – Tiếng Anh 12 (Global Success). Nội dung tự biên soạn theo định dạng đề thi tốt nghiệp THPT từ 2025.
window.QBANK = window.QBANK || [];
window.QBANK.push(
  // ===== Unit 1. Life stories we admire =====
  { id: 'anh12-1-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nMarie Curie was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize, and her ______ to science is still remembered today.",
    options: ["contribution", "distribution", "attribution", "constitution"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Cụm 'contribution to sth' = sự đóng góp cho cái gì. Distribution = sự phân phối; attribution = sự quy cho; constitution = hiến pháp – đều không hợp nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nAt 8 p.m. yesterday, I ______ a documentary about the life of a famous scientist.",
    options: ["watched", "was watching", "have watched", "am watching"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Mốc thời gian cụ thể trong quá khứ 'at 8 p.m. yesterday' → hành động đang diễn ra tại thời điểm đó dùng quá khứ tiếp diễn: was watching." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the best response to complete the exchange.\nLan: 'Who is the person you admire most?'\nMinh: '______'",
    options: ["Yes, I admire him a lot.", "I don't think so.", "It doesn't matter to me.", "My grandfather. He went through hard times but always stayed kind."], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Câu hỏi 'Who…?' cần trả lời là một người cụ thể kèm lí do → 'My grandfather…'. Các phương án còn lại dùng cho câu hỏi Yes/No hoặc không trả lời đúng câu hỏi." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe young doctor decided to work in a remote village ______.",
    options: ["because he wanted to earn a lot of money", "so that he could live in a big city", "where people had little access to health care", "which he had never wanted to help"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Mệnh đề quan hệ 'where people had little access to health care' bổ nghĩa cho 'a remote village', hợp logic (bác sĩ trẻ về làng xa nơi người dân thiếu dịch vụ y tế). A, B mâu thuẫn ý nghĩa; D sai ngữ pháp và nghĩa (which … to help)." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nHer ______ to finish her studies despite her serious illness inspired all her classmates.",
    options: ["determine", "determined", "determination", "determinedly"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Sau tính từ sở hữu 'her' và làm chủ ngữ của động từ 'inspired' cần một danh từ: determination (sự quyết tâm). 'determination to do sth' là cụm cố định." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. This is the first time I have read such a moving biography.\n→ I have never ...\n2. He was walking home. He saw an old man fall off his bike.\n→ While ...\n3. People admire her because she is very generous.\n→ She is admired for ...",
    answer: "1. I have never read such a moving biography before. 2. While he was walking home, he saw an old man fall off his bike. 3. She is admired for her (great) generosity.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu đúng 1 điểm (tổng 3 điểm).\n1. 'This is the first time + S + have/has + V3' ⇔ 'S + have/has never + V3 … before'.\n2. Hành động đang diễn ra (quá khứ tiếp diễn) bị hành động khác xen vào (quá khứ đơn): While + S + was/were + V-ing, S + V2.\n3. 'admire sb for sth' → bị động 'be admired for + danh từ'; generous (adj) → generosity (n).\nTrừ 0,25 điểm/lỗi chính tả hoặc chia động từ." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nAfter years of hard work in a small garage, the young inventor finally ______ a name for himself in the field of robotics.",
    options: ["did", "got", "took", "made"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Thành ngữ 'make a name for oneself' = trở nên nổi tiếng, tạo dựng tên tuổi. Không dùng do/get/take với 'a name' theo nghĩa này." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nWhen the journalist arrived, the old soldier ______ his medals to a group of students, so she waited until he finished.",
    options: ["was showing", "showed", "has shown", "had shown"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Khi nhà báo đến, ông cựu chiến binh đang cho học sinh xem huy chương (hành động đang diễn ra) và cô phải đợi ông xong → quá khứ tiếp diễn 'was showing'. 'had shown' (đã xong trước) mâu thuẫn với 'waited until he finished'; 'showed' chỉ hành động xảy ra sau khi cô đến." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe athlete ______ her leg while she ______ for the national competition, but she ______ to give up her dream.",
    options: ["was breaking – trained – refused", "broke – was training – refused", "broke – trained – was refusing", "had broken – was training – was refusing"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Hành động ngắn 'broke' xen vào hành động đang diễn ra 'was training' (while + quá khứ tiếp diễn); hành động tiếp theo hoàn tất trong quá khứ 'refused'. Các phương án khác dùng sai thì." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the announcement and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nTALK: HEROES NEXT DOOR\nThis Saturday, our school library is proud to welcome Mr Tran Quang, a retired firefighter with 30 years of service. He will share the stories of the people he rescued and the moments that (10) ______ his life. Students are encouraged to prepare their questions (11) ______ advance. Seats are limited, so please register at the library desk before Thursday.",
    options: ["shaped", "shaping", "to shape", "shapes"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Sau đại từ quan hệ 'that' (làm chủ ngữ) cần động từ chia thì; những khoảnh khắc trong quá khứ đã định hình cuộc đời ông → quá khứ đơn 'shaped'." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the announcement and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nTALK: HEROES NEXT DOOR\nThis Saturday, our school library is proud to welcome Mr Tran Quang, a retired firefighter with 30 years of service. He will share the stories of the people he rescued and the moments that (10) ______ his life. Students are encouraged to prepare their questions (11) ______ advance. Seats are limited, so please register at the library desk before Thursday.",
    options: ["on", "in", "at", "for"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Cụm cố định 'in advance' = trước, sẵn từ trước." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nWhen Linh was born, doctors told her parents that she would never walk. She spent her childhood in a wheelchair, but she refused to let it limit her dreams. She read every book in her village library and taught herself to code on an old laptop given by a neighbour. At nineteen, she created a mobile app that helps disabled people find wheelchair-friendly cafés and shops. Today, the app has more than 200,000 users, and Linh travels around the country giving talks to young people.\nAccording to the passage, how did Linh learn to code?",
    options: ["She attended a programming course in the city.", "Her parents hired a private tutor for her.", "She learned it at her village school.", "She studied on her own using an old laptop."], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Câu 'taught herself to code on an old laptop given by a neighbour' → cô tự học lập trình trên chiếc máy tính cũ. Bài không nhắc khóa học, gia sư hay trường làng dạy lập trình." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. However, he did not give up and opened a small food stall instead.\nb. Mr Binh lost his job at a factory when he was fifty.\nc. Today, his chain of restaurants employs over three hundred people.\nd. Thanks to his delicious recipes, the stall soon became popular.",
    options: ["a – b – d – c", "b – d – a – c", "b – a – d – c", "d – b – a – c"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Mở đầu bằng sự kiện mất việc (b) → 'However' nêu phản ứng không bỏ cuộc, mở quán (a) → 'the stall' được nhắc lại, trở nên nổi tiếng (d) → kết quả hiện nay (c). Thứ tự: b – a – d – c." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nPham Thi Thu grew up in a fishing village in central Viet Nam. Her father was often at sea, so she helped her mother sell fish at the local market before going to school every morning. Although she was always tired, Thu never missed a class, and she dreamed of becoming a nurse.\nIn 2008, a terrible storm hit her village. While the adults were trying to save their boats, fifteen-year-old Thu gathered the younger children into the village school and looked after them for two days. Her calm courage was reported in a local newspaper, and a charity offered her a scholarship to study nursing in Hue.\nThu graduated with excellent results and could have found a well-paid job in a big hospital. Instead, she returned to her village and opened a small health station. Today, she teaches villagers basic first aid and organises free health check-ups for the elderly. 'My village gave me everything,' she says. 'Now it is my turn to give something back.'",
    statements: ["Thu helped her mother at the market before school.", "During the storm, Thu helped the adults save their boats.", "Thu received a scholarship after a newspaper reported her actions.", "After graduating, Thu chose to work in a big hospital in Hue."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'she helped her mother sell fish at the local market before going to school'.\nb) Sai: người lớn cứu thuyền, còn Thu đưa trẻ nhỏ vào trường và trông chúng.\nc) Đúng: báo đưa tin → một tổ chức từ thiện trao học bổng.\nd) Sai: cô 'could have found' việc lương cao nhưng đã chọn về làng mở trạm y tế." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nWhy do we enjoy reading about the lives of other people? Psychologists suggest that life stories work like a mirror and a map at the same time. As a mirror, they let us see our own fears and hopes in someone else's experience. When we read how a famous scientist failed hundreds of times before succeeding, we feel less ashamed of our own mistakes.\nAs a map, biographies show us possible routes through life. Young readers in particular can learn how ordinary people made difficult choices, such as leaving home to study or changing careers late in life. However, experts also warn that many popular biographies present only the bright side of a person. They may hide the luck, help from others or privileges that made success possible. Readers who believe that hard work alone guarantees success may feel disappointed when real life turns out to be more complicated.\nThe best way to read a life story, therefore, is with both admiration and a critical eye.",
    statements: ["According to the passage, life stories can make readers feel less ashamed of their failures.", "The 'map' function refers to the way biographies show possible paths in life.", "The writer believes that all popular biographies are completely accurate.", "The writer implies that success may depend on more than hard work."],
    answer: [true, true, false, true],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'we feel less ashamed of our own mistakes'.\nb) Đúng: 'As a map, biographies show us possible routes through life'.\nc) Sai: tác giả cảnh báo nhiều cuốn tiểu sử chỉ nêu mặt tốt, che giấu may mắn, sự giúp đỡ… nên không hoàn toàn chính xác.\nd) Đúng (suy luận): thành công còn nhờ 'luck, help from others or privileges', nên chăm chỉ thôi chưa đảm bảo thành công." },
  { id: 'anh12-1-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-1', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Write a paragraph (120–150 words) about a person whose life story you admire. You should include:\n- who the person is and some background information,\n- the difficulties he/she faced and how he/she overcame them,\n- what you have learned from his/her life.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn 120–150 từ: giới thiệu nhân vật, khó khăn và cách vượt qua, bài học rút ra; dùng chủ yếu quá khứ đơn/quá khứ tiếp diễn.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: The person whose life story I admire most is my grandmother. She was born into a poor farming family and had to leave school at the age of twelve. While she was working in the rice fields, she taught herself to read by borrowing old newspapers from her neighbours. After the war, she opened a small tailor's shop, although she had no money and no experience. Many customers complained at first, but she never gave up and kept improving her skills. Eventually, her shop became well known in the whole district, and she earned enough to send all five children to university. From her life, I have learned that difficult beginnings do not decide our future. With determination and a love of learning, we can change our lives.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Nội dung đủ 3 ý (4 đ); Bố cục câu chủ đề – câu phát triển – câu kết, dùng từ nối (2 đ); Ngữ pháp, đặc biệt thì quá khứ (2 đ); Từ vựng phù hợp chủ đề (2 đ). Dưới 100 từ hoặc lạc đề trừ tối đa 3 đ." },

  // ===== Unit 2. A multicultural world =====
  { id: 'anh12-2-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nTet, Christmas and Diwali are important ______ festivals celebrated by different communities in our city.",
    options: ["culture", "cultural", "culturally", "cultured"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Trước danh từ 'festivals' cần tính từ: cultural (thuộc về văn hóa). 'cultured' = có học thức, tao nhã – không hợp nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nMy cousin lives in ______ United Kingdom and works as ______ engineer.",
    options: ["a – a", "Ø – an", "the – an", "the – a"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Tên nước có 'Kingdom/States/Republic' dùng 'the': the United Kingdom. 'engineer' bắt đầu bằng nguyên âm /e/ → 'an engineer'." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the utterances to make a meaningful exchange.\na. Really? What did you like most about it?\nb. I went to an international food festival last weekend.\nc. The Korean kimchi stall. I even learnt how to make kimchi!",
    options: ["b – a – c", "a – b – c", "c – a – b", "b – c – a"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Người thứ nhất kể đi lễ hội ẩm thực (b) → người thứ hai hỏi thích gì nhất (a) → người thứ nhất trả lời quầy kimchi (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nHaving lived abroad for a year, ______.",
    options: ["her English improved quickly", "it helped her understand other cultures", "the local customs no longer seemed strange to her", "she learned to respect different ways of life"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Mệnh đề phân từ 'Having lived abroad…' phải có cùng chủ ngữ (người) với mệnh đề chính → 'she learned…'. A, B, C có chủ ngữ là vật (her English, it, the local customs) → lỗi chủ ngữ treo." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThanks to the Internet, young people today are increasingly ______ to foreign music, films and fashion.",
    options: ["interested", "familiar", "aware", "exposed"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "'be exposed to sth' = được tiếp xúc với. Các từ khác đi với giới từ khác: interested in, familiar with, aware of." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. It is not necessary for visitors to take off their hats in this museum.\n→ Visitors don't ...\n2. Although she was born in Japan, she speaks Vietnamese fluently.\n→ Despite ...\n3. Globalisation has made it easier for people to try food from other countries.\n→ Thanks to ...",
    answer: "1. Visitors don't have to / don't need to take off their hats in this museum. 2. Despite being born in Japan / Despite the fact that she was born in Japan, she speaks Vietnamese fluently. 3. Thanks to globalisation, people can try food from other countries more easily.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. 'It is not necessary for sb to do' ⇔ 'sb don't have to / don't need to do'.\n2. Although + mệnh đề ⇔ Despite + V-ing/danh từ (hoặc Despite the fact that + mệnh đề).\n3. 'make it easier for sb to do' ⇔ 'Thanks to + N, sb can do … more easily'.\nChấp nhận các cách viết tương đương đúng ngữ pháp, giữ nguyên nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nWhen you travel to a new country, it is wise to follow the saying 'When in Rome, ______'.",
    options: ["do as the Romans do", "speak like the Romans", "eat what the Romans eat", "go where the Romans go"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Thành ngữ 'When in Rome, do as the Romans do' = nhập gia tùy tục. Các phương án khác không phải thành ngữ." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\n______ Mekong River flows through six countries, including Viet Nam.",
    options: ["A", "The", "An", "Ø"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Tên sông, biển, đại dương luôn dùng mạo từ 'the': the Mekong River." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Which of the following sentences is grammatically correct?",
    options: ["She sings at a international festival every year.", "The globalisation has changed the way we live.", "The Vietnamese are known for their hospitality.", "He goes to the school by the bus every day."], answer: 2,
    explanation: "'The + tính từ chỉ quốc tịch' chỉ cả dân tộc: The Vietnamese → C đúng. A sai: 'an international'. B sai: danh từ trừu tượng nói chung không dùng 'the' (Globalisation). D sai: 'go to school' (mục đích chính) và 'by bus' không có mạo từ." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the leaflet and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nINTERNATIONAL CULTURE DAY\nCome and celebrate (10) ______ diversity of our school community! Students from over ten countries will present their traditional costumes, music and food. Visitors can also take part (11) ______ workshops on calligraphy, origami and folk dancing. Entry is free for all students and parents.",
    options: ["a", "the", "an", "Ø"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'diversity' được xác định bởi cụm 'of our school community' → dùng 'the'." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the leaflet and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nINTERNATIONAL CULTURE DAY\nCome and celebrate (10) ______ diversity of our school community! Students from over ten countries will present their traditional costumes, music and food. Visitors can also take part (11) ______ workshops on calligraphy, origami and folk dancing. Entry is free for all students and parents.",
    options: ["on", "for", "in", "with"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Cụm cố định 'take part in sth' = tham gia vào." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nBanh mi is a good example of cultural blending. The baguette was introduced to Viet Nam by the French, but Vietnamese bakers made it lighter and crispier to suit the local climate and taste. They filled it with local ingredients such as pâté, pickled vegetables, coriander and chilli. Today, banh mi is sold in many cities around the world and is often seen as a symbol of Vietnamese street food.\nWhich of the following best states the main idea of the passage?",
    options: ["Banh mi shows how different cultures can blend to create something new.", "French bread is more popular than Vietnamese bread.", "Vietnamese bakers refused to follow French recipes.", "Banh mi is only sold in Viet Nam."], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Câu chủ đề 'Banh mi is a good example of cultural blending' và toàn bài mô tả sự kết hợp bánh mì Pháp với nguyên liệu Việt → A. D sai vì bánh mì bán ở nhiều thành phố trên thế giới; B, C không được nêu." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. For example, I learnt to bow slightly when greeting older people in Korea.\nb. Living in a multicultural environment has taught me many valuable lessons.\nc. Most importantly, I have become more open-minded and tolerant.\nd. First, I have learnt to respect customs that are different from mine.",
    options: ["b – a – d – c", "d – a – b – c", "b – c – d – a", "b – d – a – c"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Câu chủ đề (b) → ý thứ nhất 'First…' (d) → ví dụ minh họa 'For example…' (a) → ý quan trọng nhất, kết đoạn 'Most importantly…' (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nWhen Quan arrived in Melbourne to study engineering, everything seemed exciting. The streets were clean, people smiled at strangers, and the campus was full of students from all over the world. After a few weeks, however, the excitement faded. He missed his mother's cooking, found the local accent hard to understand and felt shy about speaking in class, where students were expected to question their lecturers.\nQuan was experiencing culture shock, a common feeling among people who move to a new country. Instead of staying in his room, he decided to join the university's international students' club. There he met Sofia from Brazil and Aiko from Japan, who were facing the same problems. Together they cooked meals from their home countries every Friday and practised English by chatting with local volunteers.\nBy the end of his first year, Quan felt at home. He still loved Vietnamese food, but he also enjoyed Australian barbecues and had learned to express his opinions confidently in class.",
    statements: ["Quan felt excited when he first arrived in Melbourne.", "Quan found it easy to understand the local accent.", "Quan joined a club and met other students with similar problems.", "By the end of the first year, Quan had stopped eating Vietnamese food."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'everything seemed exciting'.\nb) Sai: 'found the local accent hard to understand'.\nc) Đúng: anh gia nhập câu lạc bộ sinh viên quốc tế, gặp Sofia và Aiko 'facing the same problems'.\nd) Sai: 'He still loved Vietnamese food'." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nCritics of globalisation often claim that it is turning the world into one big shopping mall where everyone eats the same burgers and listens to the same songs. There is some truth in this: global brands can be found in almost every city, and young people in Ha Noi, Paris and Lima may follow the same online stars.\nYet the picture is more complex. Cultures rarely disappear simply because they meet each other; more often, they mix and change. Korean pop music, for instance, borrowed heavily from American hip-hop and pop, but it developed its own style and is now exported back to the West. Similarly, many international fast-food chains have changed their menus to suit local tastes, offering rice dishes in Asia and spicy sauces in Latin America.\nThe real danger, some researchers argue, is not that cultures will become identical, but that smaller communities may lack the resources to promote their own traditions. Without support, their languages and crafts could gradually be forgotten.",
    statements: ["The writer completely agrees that globalisation makes all cultures the same.", "K-pop is given as an example of a culture borrowing from others and creating something new.", "Some fast-food chains adapt their menus to local tastes.", "According to some researchers, small communities may struggle to keep their traditions alive."],
    answer: [false, true, true, true],
    explanation: "a) Sai: tác giả chỉ thừa nhận 'some truth', rồi khẳng định 'the picture is more complex'.\nb) Đúng: K-pop vay mượn hip-hop Mỹ nhưng phát triển phong cách riêng.\nc) Đúng: 'changed their menus to suit local tastes'.\nd) Đúng: cộng đồng nhỏ 'may lack the resources to promote their own traditions'." },
  { id: 'anh12-2-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-2', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Your foreign pen friend, Emma, wants to know about a traditional Vietnamese festival. Write an email (120–150 words) to her. You should:\n- name the festival and say when it takes place,\n- describe some typical activities or food,\n- explain why the festival is meaningful to Vietnamese people.",
    answer: "Thư 120–150 từ: lời chào, giới thiệu lễ hội (thời gian), hoạt động/món ăn tiêu biểu, ý nghĩa, lời kết.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo:\nDear Emma,\nThanks for your email. You asked about a Vietnamese festival, so let me tell you about the Mid-Autumn Festival. It takes place on the fifteenth day of the eighth lunar month, when the moon is at its brightest. On that night, children carry colourful lanterns and walk around the neighbourhood singing songs. There are also lion dances in the streets, which are really exciting to watch. Families gather to enjoy mooncakes, which are filled with lotus seeds, green beans or mixed nuts, and drink tea together. The festival is meaningful because it is a time for family reunion, and it shows how much adults care about children. If you visit Viet Nam in autumn, you should join the celebration!\nBest wishes,\nNam\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Đúng định dạng thư (mở – thân – kết) (2 đ); Đủ 3 ý yêu cầu (4 đ); Ngữ pháp (2 đ); Từ vựng, mạch lạc (2 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 3. Green living =====
  { id: 'anh12-3-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nWe should use ______ bags instead of plastic ones to reduce waste.",
    options: ["disposable", "single-use", "reusable", "harmful"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "reusable = có thể tái sử dụng, phù hợp mục đích giảm rác. disposable/single-use = dùng một lần; harmful = có hại → trái nghĩa với ý câu." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\n______ all the lights and fans, she left the classroom.",
    options: ["Turn off", "Turned off", "To have turned off", "Having turned off"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Mệnh đề phân từ hoàn thành 'Having + V3' diễn tả hành động xảy ra và hoàn tất trước hành động ở mệnh đề chính (tắt đèn rồi mới rời lớp), cùng chủ ngữ 'she'." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the best response to complete the exchange.\nTom: 'Why don't we cycle to school instead of going by motorbike?'\nHa: '______'",
    options: ["No, thanks. I'm full.", "Good idea! It's healthier and greener.", "I'm sorry to hear that.", "Yes, I did it yesterday."], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'Why don't we…?' là lời đề nghị → đáp lại bằng sự đồng ý/từ chối phù hợp: 'Good idea! …'. Các phương án khác không phù hợp ngữ cảnh." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nIf every household sorted its rubbish at source, ______.",
    options: ["the amount of waste sent to landfills would fall sharply", "the landfills will be full of plastic", "we have recycled much more paper", "there had been less pollution"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Câu điều kiện loại 2 (If + quá khứ đơn, S + would + V) → 'would fall sharply', đồng thời hợp nghĩa (phân loại rác → giảm rác chôn lấp)." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nMany cafés now offer a discount to customers who bring their own cups in an effort to ______ plastic waste.",
    options: ["cut down on", "put up with", "look forward to", "come up with"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "cut down on = cắt giảm. put up with = chịu đựng; look forward to = mong đợi; come up with = nghĩ ra – không hợp nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. After he had finished his homework, he planted some trees in the garden.\n→ Having ...\n2. She was praised because she had organised the beach clean-up campaign.\n→ She was praised for ...\n3. We should not use plastic straws in the school canteen.\n→ Plastic straws ...",
    answer: "1. Having finished his homework, he planted some trees in the garden. 2. She was praised for having organised the beach clean-up campaign. 3. Plastic straws should not be used in the school canteen.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. Rút gọn mệnh đề cùng chủ ngữ, hành động xảy ra trước → 'Having + V3'.\n2. 'praise sb for + V-ing'; hành động đã xảy ra trước → danh động từ hoàn thành 'having organised' (chấp nhận 'organising').\n3. Bị động với động từ khuyết thiếu: should not + be + V3." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nLiving a green lifestyle doesn't have to ______; small changes such as turning off unused lights can make a real difference.",
    options: ["make ends meet", "cost the earth", "pay the price", "go to waste"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Thành ngữ 'cost the earth' = rất tốn kém → sống xanh không nhất thiết tốn kém. make ends meet = xoay xở đủ sống; pay the price = trả giá; go to waste = bị lãng phí." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe factory was heavily criticised for ______ toxic waste into the river for many years.",
    options: ["dump", "to dump", "having dumped", "being dumped"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Sau giới từ 'for' cần V-ing; hành động xả thải đã xảy ra trước việc bị chỉ trích → danh động từ hoàn thành 'having dumped'. 'being dumped' là bị động, sai nghĩa (nhà máy không bị xả)." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nLinh said that she hadn't left the tap running.",
    options: ["Linh admitted leaving the tap running.", "Linh refused to leave the tap running.", "Linh was accused of leaving the tap running.", "Linh denied having left the tap running."], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Phủ nhận việc đã làm trong quá khứ: 'deny + having + V3'. A (thừa nhận) trái nghĩa; B (từ chối làm) và C (bị buộc tội) khác nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the notice and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nGREEN WEEK AT OUR SCHOOL\nFrom 10 to 15 March, our school will hold Green Week to raise (10) ______ of environmental issues. Activities include a second-hand book fair, a tree-planting day and a competition for the most (11) ______ product made from recycled materials. Bring your empty bottles and old newspapers to the school gate every morning!",
    options: ["knowledge", "attention", "awareness", "understanding"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Cụm cố định 'raise awareness of sth' = nâng cao nhận thức về điều gì." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the notice and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nGREEN WEEK AT OUR SCHOOL\nFrom 10 to 15 March, our school will hold Green Week to raise (10) ______ of environmental issues. Activities include a second-hand book fair, a tree-planting day and a competition for the most (11) ______ product made from recycled materials. Bring your empty bottles and old newspapers to the school gate every morning!",
    options: ["creation", "creatively", "create", "creative"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Sau 'the most' và trước danh từ 'product' cần tính từ dài ở dạng so sánh nhất: the most creative product." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nA zero-waste lifestyle aims to send nothing to landfills. People who follow it refuse what they do not need, reduce what they do need, reuse what they can, and recycle or compost the rest. For example, they buy food in bulk using their own containers, repair broken items instead of throwing them away, and turn kitchen scraps into fertiliser. Although it is very difficult to produce no waste at all, many families have cut their rubbish by more than half.\nAccording to the passage, what do zero-waste followers do with kitchen scraps?",
    options: ["They throw them into landfills.", "They turn them into fertiliser.", "They sell them to farmers.", "They store them in their own containers."], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Câu 'turn kitchen scraps into fertiliser' → biến thức ăn thừa thành phân bón." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. Second, they should switch off electrical devices when they are not in use.\nb. There are several simple ways families can save energy at home.\nc. By following these tips, households can lower their bills and protect the planet.\nd. First, they can replace old light bulbs with LED ones.",
    options: ["b – d – a – c", "d – b – a – c", "b – a – d – c", "b – d – c – a"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Câu chủ đề (b) → First (d) → Second (a) → kết luận 'By following these tips…' (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nTwo years ago, the Nguyen family in Da Nang decided to make their home greener. They started with small steps. Instead of buying bottled water, they installed a water filter in the kitchen. They also replaced all their old light bulbs with LED ones and began to switch off the air conditioner whenever nobody was in the room.\nThe biggest change, however, was in the way they dealt with rubbish. Mrs Lan, the mother, bought three bins: one for plastic and metal, one for paper, and one for food waste. The food waste is turned into compost, which she uses for the vegetables growing on their rooftop. The children, Bao and Vy, take the plastic and paper to a recycling point near their school every Saturday.\nThe family's electricity bill has fallen by about 30 percent, and they now throw away only one small bag of rubbish a week. 'It wasn't hard at all,' says Bao. 'We just needed to change some habits.'",
    statements: ["The Nguyen family began with small changes.", "They still buy bottled water for drinking.", "Food waste is used to make compost for their rooftop vegetables.", "Bao thinks living green was very difficult."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'They started with small steps'.\nb) Sai: 'Instead of buying bottled water, they installed a water filter'.\nc) Đúng: rác thực phẩm thành phân ủ dùng cho rau trên sân thượng.\nd) Sai: Bao nói 'It wasn't hard at all'." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\n'Fast fashion' refers to cheap, trendy clothes that are produced quickly and sold in large quantities. While shoppers enjoy low prices and constant new styles, the environmental cost is enormous. Making a single cotton T-shirt can require thousands of litres of water, and many synthetic fabrics release tiny plastic fibres when they are washed. Because the clothes are cheap, people often wear them only a few times before throwing them away.\nIn response, a growing number of young consumers are turning to 'slow fashion'. They buy fewer but better-quality items, shop at second-hand stores, and swap clothes with friends. Some even learn basic sewing so that they can repair torn jeans instead of buying new ones.\nNevertheless, slow fashion is not a perfect solution. High-quality, ethically made clothes are usually more expensive, which makes them unaffordable for many families. Experts suggest that governments should also require clothing companies to take responsibility for recycling the products they sell.",
    statements: ["Fast fashion clothes are often worn only a few times before being thrown away.", "According to the passage, synthetic fabrics release plastic fibres when washed.", "Slow fashion followers usually buy more clothes than fast fashion shoppers.", "The writer suggests that consumers alone can solve the problem of fashion waste."],
    answer: [true, true, false, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'people often wear them only a few times before throwing them away'.\nb) Đúng: 'synthetic fabrics release tiny plastic fibres when they are washed'.\nc) Sai: họ 'buy fewer but better-quality items'.\nd) Sai: đoạn cuối nêu slow fashion chưa hoàn hảo và chuyên gia đề nghị chính phủ buộc doanh nghiệp chịu trách nhiệm tái chế – tức không chỉ người tiêu dùng." },
  { id: 'anh12-3-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-3', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Write a paragraph (120–150 words) about what students can do to live a greener life at school. You may use the following cues:\n- reduce plastic waste,\n- save energy and water,\n- take part in green activities or clubs.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn 120–150 từ nêu ít nhất 3 việc học sinh có thể làm để sống xanh ở trường, có ví dụ và câu kết.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: There are several ways students can live a greener life at school. First, we should reduce plastic waste by bringing our own water bottles and lunch boxes instead of buying drinks in plastic bottles or food in foam boxes. Second, saving energy and water is easy but important. Before leaving the classroom, the last student should turn off the lights and fans, and everyone should make sure that the taps are not left running. Finally, students can join green clubs or activities such as planting trees, collecting recyclable materials or organising clean-up days around the school. These activities not only make the school cleaner but also raise everyone's awareness of environmental problems. If each student makes small changes, our school will become a greener and healthier place.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Nội dung đủ ý, có ví dụ (4 đ); Bố cục, từ nối First/Second/Finally (2 đ); Ngữ pháp (2 đ); Từ vựng chủ đề môi trường (2 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 4. Urbanisation =====
  { id: 'anh12-4-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe process in which more and more people move from rural areas to live in towns and cities is called ______.",
    options: ["industry", "tourism", "population", "urbanisation"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "urbanisation = đô thị hóa, quá trình dân cư chuyển từ nông thôn ra thành thị. Các từ khác: công nghiệp, du lịch, dân số." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe bigger the city grows, ______ the traffic becomes.",
    options: ["the worse", "the bad", "worse", "the worst"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "So sánh kép 'The + so sánh hơn …, the + so sánh hơn …' → the worse (bad – worse)." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the utterances to make a meaningful conversation.\na. Yes, but the rent is so high and the air is polluted.\nb. Do you enjoy living in Ha Noi?\nc. Well, it's exciting. There's always something to do.\nd. So would you move back to your hometown one day?\ne. Maybe, after I've saved enough money.",
    options: ["b – a – c – d – e", "c – b – a – e – d", "b – c – a – d – e", "b – c – d – a – e"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Câu hỏi (b) → trả lời mặt tích cực (c) → 'Yes, but…' bổ sung mặt tiêu cực (a) → hỏi tiếp có về quê không (d) → trả lời (e)." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nEvery year, many young people leave their villages for big cities ______.",
    options: ["in order to the better jobs", "in search of better job opportunities", "so that finding better jobs", "because of they want better jobs"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'in search of + danh từ' = để tìm kiếm. A sai (in order to + V), C sai (so that + mệnh đề), D sai (because of + danh từ, không + mệnh đề)." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nOvercrowding in cities has put great ______ on public services such as hospitals and schools.",
    options: ["weight", "pressure", "force", "power"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Collocation 'put pressure on sth' = gây áp lực lên." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. As the population of a city grows larger, the demand for housing becomes higher.\n→ The larger ...\n2. Life in the countryside is not as stressful as life in the city.\n→ Life in the city ...\n3. I have never seen such a modern city before.\n→ This is the ...",
    answer: "1. The larger the population of a city grows, the higher the demand for housing becomes. 2. Life in the city is more stressful than life in the countryside. 3. This is the most modern city (that) I have ever seen.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. So sánh kép: The + so sánh hơn + S + V, the + so sánh hơn + S + V.\n2. 'not as … as' ⇔ đảo vế với so sánh hơn 'more … than'.\n3. 'never … such a + adj + N before' ⇔ 'the + so sánh nhất + N + S + have ever + V3'." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nSome rural provinces are suffering from a ______ as their best-educated young people leave for jobs in the cities and never return.",
    options: ["traffic jam", "housing shortage", "brain drain", "urban sprawl"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "brain drain = chảy máu chất xám (người có trình độ rời đi). traffic jam = tắc đường; housing shortage = thiếu nhà ở; urban sprawl = đô thị lan rộng – đều là vấn đề của thành phố, không hợp ngữ cảnh." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nLiving costs in big cities are rising ______.",
    options: ["more and more fast", "fast and fast", "more faster", "faster and faster"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "So sánh lũy tiến với tính từ/trạng từ ngắn: 'adj-er and adj-er' → faster and faster (ngày càng nhanh)." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nAs cities expand, more and more farmland is lost.",
    options: ["The more cities expand, the more farmland is lost.", "The more cities expand, the less farmland is lost.", "Cities expand so that farmland is lost.", "The less cities expand, the more farmland is lost."], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Câu gốc: thành phố càng mở rộng thì đất nông nghiệp mất càng nhiều → so sánh kép 'The more…, the more…'. B, D ngược nghĩa; C thay đổi quan hệ thành mục đích." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the leaflet and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nMOVING TO THE CITY? READ THIS FIRST!\nThe city offers many opportunities, but it can also be a lonely place. Before you move, make sure you have found a safe place to stay and (10) ______ a monthly budget. Join local clubs to make new friends, and don't hesitate to (11) ______ for help when you need it.",
    options: ["done", "taken", "had", "planned"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Song song với 'have found' → 'have planned a monthly budget' (lập ngân sách hàng tháng). done/taken/had không kết hợp với 'a budget' theo nghĩa này." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the leaflet and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nMOVING TO THE CITY? READ THIS FIRST!\nThe city offers many opportunities, but it can also be a lonely place. Before you move, make sure you have found a safe place to stay and (10) ______ a monthly budget. Join local clubs to make new friends, and don't hesitate to (11) ______ for help when you need it.",
    options: ["ask", "demand", "require", "request"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "'ask for help' = nhờ giúp đỡ. demand/require/request là ngoại động từ, không đi với 'for' trong cấu trúc này." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nMany large cities are now building satellite towns to reduce pressure on their centres. These smaller towns, located 20 to 40 kilometres away, have their own schools, hospitals and shopping centres. They are connected to the main city by fast trains or highways, so residents can commute easily. Planners hope that this will cut traffic congestion and housing prices in the city centre.\nWhy are satellite towns built, according to the passage?",
    options: ["To attract tourists to the countryside.", "To replace the old city centre.", "To reduce pressure on the main city.", "To provide more farmland for residents."], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Câu đầu: 'building satellite towns to reduce pressure on their centres' → giảm áp lực cho thành phố chính." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. As a result, many of them end up living in crowded, poorly built houses.\nb. Every year, thousands of people move from rural areas to the cities.\nc. Governments therefore need to invest more in affordable housing.\nd. However, cities often cannot build enough homes for them.",
    options: ["b – a – d – c", "b – d – a – c", "d – b – a – c", "b – d – c – a"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Hiện tượng (b) → 'However' nêu vấn đề thiếu nhà (d) → 'As a result' hậu quả (a) → 'therefore' giải pháp (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nTwenty years ago, Hoa Binh Ward was a quiet area of rice fields on the edge of the city. Most families were farmers, and the only shop sold rice, salt and cooking oil. Today, the fields have disappeared. In their place stand apartment blocks, a shopping mall and two international schools.\nOlder residents have mixed feelings about the changes. Mr Duc, 68, sold his land to a developer and used the money to build a three-storey house and send his grandchildren to university. 'Our life is much more comfortable now,' he admits. 'But I miss the fresh air and the sound of frogs at night.'\nHis neighbour, Mrs Mai, is less positive. She says that the narrow roads cannot cope with the large number of cars and motorbikes, and that flooding has become common because there is no longer enough land to absorb rainwater. Young people, on the other hand, mostly welcome the new cafés, gyms and job opportunities.",
    statements: ["Twenty years ago, Hoa Binh Ward was mainly farmland.", "Mr Duc used money from selling his land to build a house.", "Mrs Mai thinks the roads are wide enough for today's traffic.", "According to the passage, flooding has become less common in the area."],
    answer: [true, true, false, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'a quiet area of rice fields'.\nb) Đúng: ông bán đất, lấy tiền xây nhà ba tầng.\nc) Sai: bà cho rằng 'the narrow roads cannot cope with' lượng xe.\nd) Sai: 'flooding has become common'." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nUrbanisation is often discussed as a problem, but it also brings clear benefits. People living in cities generally have better access to education, health care and jobs. Because services are concentrated in one place, it is cheaper to provide clean water, electricity and public transport to a city resident than to someone living in a remote mountain village. Cities are also centres of innovation, where new businesses and ideas develop quickly.\nThe difficulties begin when cities grow faster than planners can manage. Without proper planning, new neighbourhoods appear without drainage systems, green spaces or enough schools. Traffic congestion and air pollution increase, and poorer residents may be pushed into informal settlements on the edge of the city.\nSome experts believe the solution is not to stop people from moving to cities, which would be almost impossible, but to plan for growth in advance. This includes building public transport before neighbourhoods are filled, protecting parks and lakes, and developing smaller cities so that not everyone heads to the largest ones.",
    statements: ["The writer believes that urbanisation has no advantages.", "According to the passage, it can be cheaper to provide services to city residents than to people in remote areas.", "The writer suggests that problems arise when cities grow faster than they can be planned.", "The experts mentioned in the passage want to prevent people from moving to cities."],
    answer: [false, true, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Sai: 'it also brings clear benefits'.\nb) Đúng: 'it is cheaper to provide clean water… to a city resident than to someone living in a remote mountain village'.\nc) Đúng: 'The difficulties begin when cities grow faster than planners can manage'.\nd) Sai: họ cho rằng giải pháp 'is not to stop people from moving to cities' mà là quy hoạch trước." },
  { id: 'anh12-4-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-4', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Write a paragraph (120–150 words) about the advantages and disadvantages of living in a big city. Use comparative structures where possible.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn 120–150 từ: câu chủ đề; 2–3 ưu điểm; 2–3 nhược điểm; câu kết nêu quan điểm; có dùng cấu trúc so sánh.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: Living in a big city has both advantages and disadvantages. On the one hand, city dwellers have better access to good schools, modern hospitals and a wider range of jobs than people in the countryside. Entertainment is also more varied, with cinemas, museums and shopping centres open until late at night. On the other hand, city life can be stressful. The more people move to the city, the more crowded it becomes, and traffic jams are getting worse and worse. In addition, the air in big cities is usually more polluted, and housing is much more expensive than in rural areas. In my opinion, a big city is an ideal place for young people to study and build a career, but it is not always the best place to live a peaceful life.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Nội dung cân đối ưu/nhược (4 đ); Dùng ít nhất 2 cấu trúc so sánh đúng (2 đ); Bố cục, từ nối (2 đ); Ngữ pháp, từ vựng (2 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 5. The world of work =====
  { id: 'anh12-5-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nBefore applying for a job, you should prepare a ______, which is a document listing your education, skills and work experience.",
    options: ["CV", "contract", "salary", "reference"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "CV (curriculum vitae) = sơ yếu lí lịch, liệt kê học vấn, kĩ năng, kinh nghiệm. contract = hợp đồng; salary = lương; reference = thư giới thiệu." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe manager ______ interviewed me yesterday was very friendly.",
    options: ["which", "who", "whose", "whom"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Đại từ quan hệ thay cho người, làm chủ ngữ của 'interviewed' → who. 'whom' chỉ làm tân ngữ; 'which' chỉ vật; 'whose' chỉ sở hữu." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the best response to complete the exchange in a job interview.\nInterviewer: 'What would you say are your main strengths?'\nCandidate: '______'",
    options: ["I don't know, really.", "My salary should be high.", "Yes, of course I'm strong.", "I'm hard-working, and I communicate well with others."], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Câu hỏi về điểm mạnh → nêu phẩm chất, kĩ năng cụ thể: 'I'm hard-working…'. C hiểu sai 'strengths' (sức mạnh thể chất) và trả lời Yes/No không phù hợp." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nShe was offered the position ______.",
    options: ["although she had all the skills needed", "because she was too inexperienced", "because her experience matched the requirements perfectly", "so she was very good at teamwork"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Được nhận việc vì kinh nghiệm phù hợp hoàn toàn với yêu cầu → C. A, B mâu thuẫn logic; D sai quan hệ nhân – quả." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nNurses and doctors often work ______ hours, including nights, weekends and public holidays.",
    options: ["short", "full", "irregular", "spare"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "irregular hours = giờ giấc thất thường, phù hợp với 'nights, weekends and public holidays'. 'spare hours' = giờ rảnh; 'full hours' không phải collocation." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Combine or rewrite the sentences as instructed, beginning with the given words.\n1. My aunt is a nurse. She works night shifts at the city hospital. (Use a non-defining relative clause.)\n→ My aunt, ...\n2. This is the company. I did my internship there last summer.\n→ This is the company where ...\n3. He started working for this firm five years ago.\n→ He has ...",
    answer: "1. My aunt, who works night shifts at the city hospital, is a nurse. 2. This is the company where I did my internship last summer. 3. He has worked / has been working for this firm for five years.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. Mệnh đề quan hệ không xác định đặt giữa hai dấu phẩy, dùng 'who' (không dùng 'that').\n2. 'where' thay cho 'there' (trạng từ nơi chốn); không giữ lại 'there'.\n3. 'started … ago' ⇔ hiện tại hoàn thành + for + khoảng thời gian." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nAfter two years of excellent performance, Nam was finally ______ to team leader.",
    options: ["raised", "increased", "lifted", "promoted"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "'be promoted to + vị trí' = được thăng chức. raised/increased dùng cho lương, giá; lifted = nhấc lên." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nApplicants ______ CVs are incomplete will not be invited to the interview.",
    options: ["whose", "who", "which", "whom"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Giữa danh từ chỉ người 'Applicants' và danh từ 'CVs' cần đại từ quan hệ chỉ sở hữu → whose (CV của những ứng viên)." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Which of the following sentences is grammatically correct?",
    options: ["The job, that I applied for last month, is well paid.", "Mr Long, who has worked here for 20 years, is retiring next month.", "The office where I work in is near my house.", "The candidate whom got the job is my cousin."], answer: 1,
    explanation: "B đúng: mệnh đề không xác định với 'who'. A sai: không dùng 'that' trong mệnh đề không xác định. C sai: 'where' đã bao hàm giới từ, phải bỏ 'in' (hoặc dùng 'which … in'). D sai: làm chủ ngữ phải dùng 'who'." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the advertisement and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nWE'RE HIRING!\nSunny Café is looking for part-time staff (10) ______ are friendly, reliable and able to work at weekends. No experience is required, (11) ______ full training will be provided. To apply, send your CV to the address below before 30 June.",
    options: ["who", "which", "whose", "where"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Thay cho danh từ chỉ người 'staff', làm chủ ngữ của 'are' → who." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the advertisement and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nWE'RE HIRING!\nSunny Café is looking for part-time staff (10) ______ are friendly, reliable and able to work at weekends. No experience is required, (11) ______ full training will be provided. To apply, send your CV to the address below before 30 June.",
    options: ["unless", "as", "so", "although"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Không cần kinh nghiệm VÌ sẽ được đào tạo đầy đủ → 'as' (= because). 'so' đảo ngược quan hệ nhân quả; 'although' mang nghĩa nhượng bộ không hợp; 'unless' sai nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nRemote work became common during the pandemic, and many companies have kept it since then. Employees save time on commuting and can organise their day more flexibly. However, some workers report feeling isolated and find it hard to separate work from family life. To solve this, several companies now use a 'hybrid' model, in which staff work from home for part of the week and come to the office on the other days.\nWhat is the 'hybrid' model, according to the passage?",
    options: ["Working only from home.", "Working for two different companies.", "Working night shifts and day shifts.", "Combining working from home and working at the office."], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Câu cuối: 'staff work from home for part of the week and come to the office on the other days' → kết hợp làm ở nhà và ở văn phòng." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful letter of application.\nDear Sir or Madam,\na. I am writing to apply for the position of part-time sales assistant advertised on your website.\nb. I look forward to hearing from you.\nc. Last summer, I worked at a bookshop, where I developed good communication skills.\nd. I believe this experience makes me a suitable candidate for the job.\nYours faithfully,\nTran Minh Anh",
    options: ["a – d – c – b", "c – a – d – b", "a – c – d – b", "a – c – b – d"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Nêu mục đích viết thư (a) → kinh nghiệm (c) → 'this experience' nhắc lại ý trước, khẳng định sự phù hợp (d) → câu kết thư (b)." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nLast summer, Khanh, a Grade 11 student, did a four-week internship at a small travel agency in Hoi An. On his first day, he was nervous because he had never worked in an office before. His supervisor, Ms Thuy, gave him simple tasks such as answering emails and updating the company's social media page.\nAfter a week, Khanh was asked to help with a tour for a group of Australian visitors. He had to explain the history of the old town in English, which was a big challenge. He prepared carefully every evening, and by the end of the tour, the visitors thanked him warmly and left a five-star review online.\nKhanh did not receive a salary, but the company paid for his lunch and transport. More importantly, he discovered what he wants to do in the future. 'I used to think tourism was just about travelling,' he says. 'Now I know it requires planning, communication skills and a lot of patience.' He now plans to study tourism management at university.",
    statements: ["Khanh had worked in an office before his internship.", "Ms Thuy first gave Khanh simple tasks.", "Khanh received a monthly salary from the travel agency.", "The internship helped Khanh decide on his future studies."],
    answer: [false, true, false, true],
    explanation: "a) Sai: 'he had never worked in an office before'.\nb) Đúng: 'gave him simple tasks such as answering emails…'.\nc) Sai: 'Khanh did not receive a salary'.\nd) Đúng: cậu dự định học quản trị du lịch ở đại học." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nWhen employers are asked what they look for in young workers, they rarely mention exam results first. Instead, they talk about 'soft skills' – abilities such as communication, teamwork, problem-solving and time management. Unlike technical knowledge, which can often be taught on the job in a few weeks, soft skills develop slowly through experience.\nThis creates a challenge for school-leavers. Many have excellent grades but little experience of working in a team or dealing with customers. Some employers say that new graduates struggle to accept criticism or to manage their own workload without detailed instructions.\nThe good news is that soft skills can be developed while still at school. Taking part in clubs, volunteering, doing part-time jobs and organising school events all give young people chances to practise them. Students who can describe such experiences clearly in a job interview often stand out from candidates who list only their qualifications. In today's job market, what you can do with others may matter as much as what you know.",
    statements: ["According to the passage, employers usually mention exam results before soft skills.", "Technical knowledge can often be learned at work more quickly than soft skills.", "Some new graduates find it difficult to work without detailed instructions.", "The writer suggests that qualifications are now completely unimportant."],
    answer: [false, true, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Sai: 'they rarely mention exam results first'.\nb) Đúng: kiến thức kĩ thuật 'can often be taught on the job in a few weeks', còn kĩ năng mềm 'develop slowly'.\nc) Đúng: 'struggle… to manage their own workload without detailed instructions'.\nd) Sai: câu cuối nói kĩ năng làm việc với người khác 'may matter as much as what you know' – tức kiến thức vẫn quan trọng." },
  { id: 'anh12-5-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-5', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "You have seen the following advertisement:\nSUMMER CAMP ASSISTANTS WANTED – We need energetic students aged 16–18 to help organise activities for children aged 8–12 from 1 to 31 July. Good English required.\nWrite a letter of application (120–150 words) to the camp director, Ms Hanh. In your letter, you should:\n- say which position you are applying for and where you saw the advertisement,\n- describe your relevant skills and experience,\n- say when you are available for an interview.",
    answer: "Thư xin việc 120–150 từ, văn phong trang trọng: mục đích, kĩ năng/kinh nghiệm phù hợp, thời gian phỏng vấn, kết thư lịch sự.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo:\nDear Ms Hanh,\nI am writing to apply for the position of summer camp assistant, which I saw advertised on your website last week. I am seventeen years old and a Grade 11 student at Le Loi High School.\nI believe I would be a suitable candidate for this job. I have been a member of my school's volunteer club for two years, and I regularly help organise games and art activities for children at a local community centre. Through this experience, I have become patient, responsible and good at working in a team. In addition, my English is quite good, as I achieved a high score in the school English competition.\nI am available for an interview any weekday afternoon after 4 p.m. I look forward to hearing from you.\nYours sincerely,\nNguyen Thu Trang\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Định dạng & văn phong trang trọng (2 đ); Đủ 3 ý (4 đ); Ngữ pháp, có dùng mệnh đề quan hệ (2 đ); Từ vựng chủ đề việc làm (2 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 6. Artificial intelligence =====
  { id: 'anh12-6-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nA ______ is a machine that can carry out a series of tasks automatically, sometimes in place of humans.",
    options: ["program", "robot", "screen", "network"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "robot = người máy, cỗ máy tự động thực hiện công việc. program = chương trình; screen = màn hình; network = mạng lưới." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nNowadays, many dangerous tasks in factories ______ by robots.",
    options: ["do", "are doing", "are done", "have done"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Chủ ngữ 'tasks' chịu tác động (được robot làm), có 'by robots' → bị động hiện tại đơn: are done." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the utterances to make a meaningful conversation.\na. It's an AI app that helps me practise speaking English.\nb. What are you using on your phone?\nc. Sounds useful. Does it correct your pronunciation?\nd. Yes, and it gives me feedback instantly.",
    options: ["b – a – c – d", "b – c – a – d", "a – b – c – d", "b – a – d – c"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Câu hỏi (b) → trả lời giới thiệu ứng dụng (a) → nhận xét và hỏi tiếp (c) → trả lời 'Yes…' (d)." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nSmart speakers can understand and respond to voice commands, ______.",
    options: ["which make life is more convenient", "that making life more convenient", "what makes life more convenient", "which makes life more convenient"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Mệnh đề quan hệ 'which' sau dấu phẩy thay cho cả mệnh đề trước, động từ chia số ít: which makes. A thừa 'is', B sai dạng động từ và không dùng 'that' sau dấu phẩy, C 'what' không dùng làm đại từ quan hệ." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nSelf-driving cars use sensors and cameras to ______ obstacles on the road and avoid accidents.",
    options: ["invent", "produce", "create", "detect"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "detect = phát hiện. Xe tự lái dùng cảm biến để phát hiện chướng ngại vật; invent/produce/create = phát minh/sản xuất/tạo ra – không hợp nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. Engineers will develop a new AI system for hospitals next year.\n→ A new AI system ...\n2. People say that AI will replace many jobs in the future.\n→ It is said ...\n3. A technician repaired my laptop yesterday.\n→ I had ...",
    answer: "1. A new AI system for hospitals will be developed (by engineers) next year. 2. It is said that AI will replace many jobs in the future. 3. I had my laptop repaired (by a technician) yesterday.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. Bị động tương lai đơn: will be + V3.\n2. Bị động khách quan: People say that + mệnh đề ⇔ It is said that + mệnh đề (hoặc AI is said to replace…).\n3. Thể nhờ bảo (causative): have + sth + V3." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nMany experts describe AI as a ______ sword: it brings huge benefits but also serious risks.",
    options: ["double-edged", "two-sided", "double-faced", "two-handed"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Thành ngữ 'a double-edged sword' = con dao hai lưỡi (vừa có lợi vừa có hại)." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nAI is expected ______ doctors diagnose diseases more accurately in the future.",
    options: ["helping", "to help", "to be helped", "helped"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Cấu trúc bị động khách quan: S + be + expected + to V (hành động ở tương lai, AI chủ động giúp) → to help." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nPeople think that the robot was designed by a group of students.",
    options: ["The robot thinks it was designed by a group of students.", "It was thought that a group of students designs the robot.", "The robot is thought to have been designed by a group of students.", "A group of students is thought to design the robot."], answer: 2,
    explanation: "'think' ở hiện tại, hành động thiết kế xảy ra trước và ở thể bị động → S + is thought + to have been + V3. B, D sai thì; A sai nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the announcement and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nAI WORKSHOP FOR TEENS\nCurious about how chatbots work? Join our free two-day workshop! You will learn the basics of machine learning and (10) ______ your own simple chatbot. Laptops will be (11) ______ by the organisers, so you just need to bring your curiosity!",
    options: ["make up", "build", "set off", "grow"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'build a chatbot' = xây dựng/tạo một chatbot. make up = bịa ra; set off = khởi hành; grow = trồng, lớn lên." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the announcement and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nAI WORKSHOP FOR TEENS\nCurious about how chatbots work? Join our free two-day workshop! You will learn the basics of machine learning and (10) ______ your own simple chatbot. Laptops will be (11) ______ by the organisers, so you just need to bring your curiosity!",
    options: ["provide", "providing", "provided", "provision"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Bị động tương lai 'will be + V3' (máy tính được ban tổ chức cung cấp) → provided." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nOn some farms, drones equipped with AI cameras fly over the fields to check the health of the crops. The software can spot signs of disease or lack of water long before humans notice them. Farmers then receive alerts on their phones and treat only the affected areas, which saves water, fertiliser and money.\nWhat is the main benefit of AI drones mentioned in the passage?",
    options: ["They help farmers find and treat problems early while saving resources.", "They completely replace farmers in the fields.", "They plant crops faster than humans.", "They sell crops directly to customers."], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Drone phát hiện bệnh/thiếu nước sớm, nông dân chỉ xử lý vùng bị ảnh hưởng → tiết kiệm nước, phân bón, tiền → A. Các ý khác không được nêu." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. For instance, students can receive personalised exercises based on their level.\nb. On the other hand, relying too much on AI may weaken students' critical thinking.\nc. AI tools are changing the way students learn.\nd. Therefore, schools should teach students how to use AI wisely.",
    options: ["c – b – a – d", "a – c – b – d", "c – a – d – b", "c – a – b – d"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Câu chủ đề (c) → ví dụ lợi ích 'For instance' (a) → mặt trái 'On the other hand' (b) → kết luận 'Therefore' (d)." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nAt Riverside Hospital, a new AI system has been helping doctors read X-ray images since last year. The system was trained on more than a million images, so it can recognise early signs of lung disease within seconds. Before it was introduced, patients sometimes had to wait two or three days for their results. Now most of them receive a report on the same day.\nDr Hung, who leads the radiology department, stresses that the AI does not make the final decision. 'It acts like a second pair of eyes,' he explains. 'When the system marks an image as unusual, one of our doctors always checks it carefully.' In a few cases, the AI has made mistakes, for example by confusing an old scar with a new infection.\nThe hospital now plans to use similar technology to analyse heart scans. However, it has promised that patients' personal data will be protected and that doctors will continue to meet every patient face to face.",
    statements: ["The AI system was trained on over a million X-ray images.", "Since the AI system was introduced, patients have had to wait longer for their results.", "According to Dr Hung, the AI system makes the final diagnosis.", "The AI system has occasionally made mistakes."],
    answer: [true, false, false, true],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'trained on more than a million images'.\nb) Sai: trước phải chờ 2–3 ngày, nay đa số nhận kết quả trong ngày.\nc) Sai: 'the AI does not make the final decision'.\nd) Đúng: 'In a few cases, the AI has made mistakes'." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nSince AI chatbots became widely available, teachers around the world have been debating whether students should be allowed to use them. Supporters point out that a chatbot can explain a difficult idea in several different ways, answer questions at midnight and give instant feedback on a piece of writing. For shy students, asking a machine may feel less embarrassing than raising a hand in class.\nCritics, however, worry that students will simply copy answers without understanding them. They also note that chatbots sometimes produce information that sounds convincing but is completely wrong. A student who trusts every answer may end up learning false facts.\nMany schools are now trying a middle path. Instead of banning chatbots, they ask students to show how they used them – for example, by submitting the questions they asked and explaining how they checked the answers. In this way, AI becomes a tool for thinking rather than a replacement for it. As one teacher put it, 'The question is not whether students use AI, but how they use it.'",
    statements: ["Supporters believe chatbots can give students quick feedback.", "According to the passage, chatbots always provide accurate information.", "The 'middle path' means that schools completely ban chatbots.", "The teacher quoted at the end believes the way students use AI matters most."],
    answer: [true, false, false, true],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'give instant feedback on a piece of writing'.\nb) Sai: chatbot đôi khi đưa thông tin 'completely wrong'.\nc) Sai: 'Instead of banning chatbots…' – họ cho phép nhưng yêu cầu trình bày cách dùng.\nd) Đúng: 'The question is not whether students use AI, but how they use it'." },
  { id: 'anh12-6-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-6', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Some people believe that artificial intelligence will make our lives better, while others worry about its negative effects. Write a paragraph (120–150 words) giving your opinion on the benefits and risks of AI in everyday life.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn nghị luận 120–150 từ: nêu quan điểm, 2 lợi ích, 1–2 rủi ro, đề xuất/kết luận.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: In my opinion, artificial intelligence will make our lives better as long as it is used responsibly. First, AI can save us a great deal of time. Smart assistants can set reminders, translate languages instantly and suggest the fastest route to school or work. Second, AI is widely used in health care, where it helps doctors detect diseases earlier and more accurately. However, AI also brings some risks. Many routine jobs may be replaced by machines, and people who rely too much on AI tools might stop thinking for themselves. Moreover, personal data collected by AI systems could be stolen or misused. Therefore, governments should introduce clear rules to protect users, and schools should teach students to use AI wisely. If we do this, AI will be a helpful tool rather than a threat.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Quan điểm rõ ràng (1 đ); Lập luận có lợi ích và rủi ro kèm ví dụ (4 đ); Từ nối, bố cục (2 đ); Ngữ pháp – có thể dùng câu bị động (2 đ); Từ vựng chủ đề (1 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 7. The world of mass media =====
  { id: 'anh12-7-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nNewspapers, television, radio and the Internet are all forms of ______, which reach a large number of people at the same time.",
    options: ["social clubs", "advertising", "mass media", "entertainment"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "mass media = phương tiện truyền thông đại chúng, tiếp cận số đông cùng lúc." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe news programme ______ on VTV1 at 7 p.m. every evening attracts millions of viewers.",
    options: ["broadcasts", "is broadcast", "to broadcast", "broadcast"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Rút gọn mệnh đề quan hệ bị động 'which is broadcast' → quá khứ phân từ 'broadcast' (broadcast – broadcast – broadcast). Câu đã có động từ chính 'attracts' nên không thể dùng A hoặc B." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the best response to complete the exchange.\nPeter: 'I think social media is the best source of news nowadays.'\nMai: '______'",
    options: ["You're welcome.", "I'm not so sure. A lot of fake news spreads there.", "That's very kind of you.", "Yes, please."], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Đáp lại một ý kiến → bày tỏ đồng tình/phản đối kèm lí do: 'I'm not so sure. …'. Các phương án khác dùng để đáp lời cảm ơn, lời khen hay lời mời." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nBefore sharing a news story online, ______.",
    options: ["you should check whether it comes from a reliable source", "the source must check it carefully by itself", "checking the source is not necessary at all", "the news is always true"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Lời khuyên hợp lí và đúng chủ ngữ (người chia sẻ là 'you'): kiểm tra nguồn tin trước khi chia sẻ. Các phương án còn lại sai logic hoặc lỗi chủ ngữ." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nA ______ is a misleading title designed to make readers click on an article, even when the content is disappointing.",
    options: ["clickbait headline", "breaking news", "weekly column", "subscription"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "clickbait headline = tiêu đề giật tít để câu lượt nhấp. breaking news = tin nóng; column = chuyên mục; subscription = gói đăng kí." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. The article which was written by a Grade 12 student won the first prize.\n→ The article written ...\n2. People who use social media should think carefully before posting.\n→ People using ...\n3. Although the story was fake, it was shared thousands of times.\n→ Despite ...",
    answer: "1. The article written by a Grade 12 student won the first prize. 2. People using social media should think carefully before posting. 3. Despite being fake / Despite the fact that it was fake, the story was shared thousands of times.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. Rút gọn mệnh đề quan hệ bị động: bỏ 'which was', giữ V3.\n2. Rút gọn mệnh đề quan hệ chủ động: bỏ 'who', V → V-ing.\n3. Although + mệnh đề ⇔ Despite + V-ing / Despite the fact that + mệnh đề." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nInfluencers who promote products without telling their followers that they are paid are not being ______ with their audience.",
    options: ["broad", "upfront", "outgoing", "straight away"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'be upfront with sb' = thẳng thắn, minh bạch với ai. outgoing = hướng ngoại; straight away = ngay lập tức; broad = rộng." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nMost teenagers today get their news from social media ______ from printed newspapers.",
    options: ["instead", "in spite of", "rather than", "because of"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "'rather than' = thay vì, nối hai thành phần song song (from social media / from printed newspapers). 'instead' cần 'of'; in spite of/because of sai nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best combines the two sentences.\nThe documentary was very interesting. Millions of people watched it.",
    options: ["The documentary which millions of people watched it was very interesting.", "Watching by millions of people, the documentary was very interesting.", "The documentary watched millions of people was very interesting.", "The documentary, which was watched by millions of people, was very interesting."], answer: 3,
    explanation: "D đúng: mệnh đề quan hệ bị động không xác định. A thừa 'it'; B sai dạng phân từ (phải là 'Watched'); C thiếu 'by', sai nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the notice and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nSCHOOL RADIO CLUB – NEW MEMBERS WANTED\nDo you love talking, writing scripts or (10) ______ music? Our radio club produces a 15-minute show every Friday lunchtime. No experience is necessary. We will teach you how to use the recording equipment (11) ______ you can start producing shows quickly. Come to Room 204 on Monday at 4 p.m. to find out more.",
    options: ["edit", "edited", "editing", "to edit"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Cấu trúc song song sau 'love': talking, writing scripts or editing music." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the notice and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nSCHOOL RADIO CLUB – NEW MEMBERS WANTED\nDo you love talking, writing scripts or (10) ______ music? Our radio club produces a 15-minute show every Friday lunchtime. No experience is necessary. We will teach you how to use the recording equipment (11) ______ you can start producing shows quickly. Come to Room 204 on Monday at 4 p.m. to find out more.",
    options: ["because", "although", "unless", "so that"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "'so that + S + can + V' chỉ mục đích: dạy dùng thiết bị để các bạn có thể sớm làm chương trình." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nPodcasts have become one of the fastest-growing forms of media. Unlike radio programmes, which are broadcast at fixed times, podcasts can be downloaded and listened to whenever people want. Many listeners enjoy them while commuting, exercising or doing housework. Because they are cheap to produce, anyone with a microphone and an idea can start one.\nAccording to the passage, how are podcasts different from radio programmes?",
    options: ["They are more expensive to produce.", "They can be listened to at any time.", "They are only about music.", "They are broadcast at fixed times."], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'Unlike radio programmes, which are broadcast at fixed times, podcasts can be… listened to whenever people want' → nghe bất cứ lúc nào. D là đặc điểm của radio; A trái với 'cheap to produce'." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. First, check who wrote the story and when it was published.\nb. Fake news can spread very quickly, so it is important to know how to spot it.\nc. Finally, compare the story with reports from trusted news websites.\nd. Next, look carefully at the headline and the photos.",
    options: ["b – a – d – c", "b – d – a – c", "a – b – d – c", "b – a – c – d"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Câu chủ đề (b) → First (a) → Next (d) → Finally (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nMy grandfather still reads a printed newspaper every morning. He walks to the kiosk at the end of our street, buys a copy and reads it slowly over a cup of tea. He says that holding the paper helps him concentrate, and he likes cutting out interesting articles to keep in a folder.\nMy parents, on the other hand, read the news on their phones while having breakfast. My mother subscribes to an online newspaper, while my father mainly watches short news videos. They both admit that they often read only the headlines.\nAs for me, I usually find out what is happening through social media. I follow several news pages, but I have learned to be careful. Last year, I shared a story about a famous singer's death, which turned out to be completely false. Since then, I always check whether a story has been reported by at least two reliable sources before I believe it – or share it.",
    statements: ["The writer's grandfather reads the news on his phone.", "The writer's mother subscribes to an online newspaper.", "The writer's parents say they always read articles in full.", "The writer once shared a false story on social media."],
    answer: [false, true, false, true],
    explanation: "a) Sai: ông đọc báo in mua ở ki-ốt.\nb) Đúng: 'My mother subscribes to an online newspaper'.\nc) Sai: 'they often read only the headlines'.\nd) Đúng: đã chia sẻ tin giả về cái chết của một ca sĩ." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nEvery time you open a social media app, an algorithm decides what you will see. These algorithms learn from your behaviour: which posts you like, how long you watch a video and what you share. Their main goal is to keep you on the platform as long as possible, because more time spent means more advertisements viewed.\nThis can create what is known as a 'filter bubble'. If you often click on stories that support a particular opinion, the algorithm will show you more of the same and fewer stories that challenge your view. Over time, you may start to believe that everyone thinks the way you do. Researchers worry that filter bubbles can make societies more divided and make people less willing to listen to others.\nEscaping the bubble is not impossible. Users can follow sources with different viewpoints, search for news directly instead of relying on their feed, and occasionally clear their viewing history. Above all, being aware that the feed is selected for you is the first step towards thinking more independently.",
    statements: ["According to the passage, algorithms learn from users' online behaviour.", "The main goal of the algorithms is to show users balanced information.", "A filter bubble may cause people to think that most others share their opinions.", "The writer suggests that it is impossible to escape a filter bubble."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'These algorithms learn from your behaviour'.\nb) Sai: mục tiêu chính là giữ người dùng ở lại lâu để xem quảng cáo.\nc) Đúng: 'you may start to believe that everyone thinks the way you do'.\nd) Sai: 'Escaping the bubble is not impossible' và tác giả đưa ra cách thoát." },
  { id: 'anh12-7-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-7', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Write a paragraph (120–150 words) giving advice to teenagers on how to use social media responsibly. You may include:\n- checking information before sharing,\n- protecting personal information,\n- managing screen time.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn 120–150 từ: câu chủ đề, ít nhất 3 lời khuyên có giải thích, câu kết.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: Social media is a powerful tool, but teenagers need to use it responsibly. First of all, we should check information carefully before sharing it. A shocking headline may be fake news, so it is wise to look for the same story on reliable news websites. Secondly, we must protect our personal information. Posting our home address, phone number or school timetable publicly can put us in danger, so we should adjust our privacy settings and only accept friend requests from people we know. Finally, it is important to manage our screen time. Spending hours scrolling through endless videos can harm our sleep and our studies. Setting a daily time limit or turning off notifications during homework can help. By following these simple rules, teenagers can enjoy social media safely and wisely.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Nội dung đủ ý, có giải thích (4 đ); Bố cục, từ nối (2 đ); Ngữ pháp (2 đ); Từ vựng chủ đề truyền thông (2 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 8. Wildlife conservation =====
  { id: 'anh12-8-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nA species that has very few individuals left and may soon disappear completely is described as ______.",
    options: ["extinct", "wild", "domestic", "endangered"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "endangered = có nguy cơ tuyệt chủng (vẫn còn một số cá thể). extinct = đã tuyệt chủng; wild = hoang dã; domestic = được thuần hóa." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nBy 2050, many animal species ______ extinct if we do not take action now.",
    options: ["will have become", "have become", "had become", "are becoming"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "'By + mốc thời gian tương lai' → tương lai hoàn thành: will have + V3 (will have become)." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the best response to complete the exchange.\nRanger: 'Please don't feed the monkeys. Human food can make them sick.'\nVisitor: '______'",
    options: ["Never mind.", "Yes, I'd love to.", "Oh, I didn't know that. Thanks for telling me.", "Congratulations!"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Đáp lại lời nhắc nhở/cảnh báo → thừa nhận và cảm ơn: 'Oh, I didn't know that. Thanks for telling me.'" },
  { id: 'anh12-8-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nRhinos are hunted illegally ______.",
    options: ["because of their horns are valuable", "for their horns, which are sold at very high prices", "although their horns are worthless", "in order to protecting them"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'for + danh từ' chỉ lí do/mục đích săn, kèm mệnh đề quan hệ 'which are sold…' → B. A sai (because of + mệnh đề), C sai nghĩa, D sai ngữ pháp (in order to + V nguyên mẫu) và nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe government has created a national park to protect the natural ______ of several rare bird species.",
    options: ["house", "habitat", "inhabitant", "habit"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "natural habitat = môi trường sống tự nhiên. inhabitant = cư dân; habit = thói quen; house = ngôi nhà (của người)." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. Scientists started studying this turtle species ten years ago, and they are still studying it.\n→ Scientists have been ...\n2. Poaching must be stopped, or elephants will disappear from the region.\n→ If poaching ...\n3. The volunteers will finish counting the birds before noon.\n→ By noon, ...",
    answer: "1. Scientists have been studying this turtle species for ten years. 2. If poaching is not stopped, elephants will disappear from the region. 3. By noon, the volunteers will have finished counting the birds.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. Hành động bắt đầu trong quá khứ, còn tiếp diễn → hiện tại hoàn thành tiếp diễn + for.\n2. 'must…, or…' ⇔ câu điều kiện loại 1 phủ định (chấp nhận 'Unless poaching is stopped' nếu đề không giới hạn từ đầu – ở đây bắt đầu bằng 'If').\n3. 'before/by + mốc tương lai' → tương lai hoàn thành: will have + V3." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nPangolins are among the most illegally ______ mammals in the world, as there is high demand for their scales and meat.",
    options: ["endangering", "dangerous", "trafficked", "protective"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "'illegally trafficked' = bị buôn bán trái phép, phù hợp với 'high demand for their scales and meat'. endangering = gây nguy hiểm; dangerous = nguy hiểm; protective = có tính bảo vệ." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nPlease don't call me at 9 a.m. tomorrow. I ______ a talk on saving sea turtles at that time.",
    options: ["give", "will have given", "have given", "will be giving"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Hành động đang diễn ra tại một thời điểm xác định trong tương lai (9 a.m. tomorrow) → tương lai tiếp diễn: will be giving." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nSo far, volunteers have planted 5,000 trees in the forest. They will plant another 5,000 before the end of the year.",
    options: ["By the end of the year, volunteers will have planted 10,000 trees in the forest.", "By the end of the year, volunteers will be planting 5,000 trees in the forest.", "Volunteers had planted 10,000 trees in the forest by the end of last year.", "Volunteers will plant only 5,000 trees in the forest this year in total."], answer: 0,
    explanation: "5,000 đã trồng + 5,000 sẽ trồng = 10,000 cây vào cuối năm → tương lai hoàn thành 'will have planted 10,000 trees'. Các phương án khác sai số lượng hoặc thì." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the leaflet and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nADOPT A TURTLE!\nFor just 200,000 VND, you can (10) ______ a sea turtle at our rescue centre for one year. Your money will be used to provide food, medical care and a safe place for injured turtles (11) ______ they are strong enough to return to the ocean. You will receive a certificate and monthly updates by email.",
    options: ["adapt", "adept", "adjust", "adopt"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "adopt = nhận nuôi (ở đây là bảo trợ một con rùa). adapt = thích nghi; adept = thành thạo (tính từ); adjust = điều chỉnh." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the leaflet and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nADOPT A TURTLE!\nFor just 200,000 VND, you can (10) ______ a sea turtle at our rescue centre for one year. Your money will be used to provide food, medical care and a safe place for injured turtles (11) ______ they are strong enough to return to the ocean. You will receive a certificate and monthly updates by email.",
    options: ["until", "since", "unless", "while"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "'until' = cho đến khi: chăm sóc rùa bị thương cho đến khi chúng đủ khỏe để trở về biển." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nThe saola, sometimes called the 'Asian unicorn', was discovered in the forests along the border between Viet Nam and Laos in 1992. It is one of the rarest mammals on Earth, and scientists have very rarely seen it in the wild. The main threat to the saola is snares – simple wire traps set by hunters to catch other animals. Conservation groups have removed thousands of these traps from the forests.\nWhat is the main threat to the saola mentioned in the passage?",
    options: ["Forest fires.", "Climate change.", "Wire traps set by hunters.", "A lack of food."], answer: 2,
    explanation: "'The main threat to the saola is snares – simple wire traps set by hunters' → bẫy dây thép của thợ săn." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. Their numbers have dropped sharply due to habitat loss and poaching.\nb. Wild elephants were once common in many parts of Viet Nam.\nc. If nothing is done, they may disappear from the country completely.\nd. Today, only around one hundred are believed to remain in the wild.",
    options: ["b – d – a – c", "b – a – d – c", "a – b – d – c", "b – a – c – d"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Quá khứ phổ biến (b) → số lượng giảm mạnh và nguyên nhân (a) → hiện nay chỉ còn khoảng 100 cá thể (d) → cảnh báo tương lai (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nLast July, twenty students from our school spent a week volunteering at a wildlife rescue centre in the north of Viet Nam. The centre cares for animals that have been saved from illegal traders, including bears, monkeys and pangolins. Most of the animals arrive injured, frightened and very thin.\nOur main job was to prepare food. Every morning, we chopped fruit and vegetables for the monkeys and mixed special food for the bears. We were not allowed to touch the animals, because the staff want them to stay wild so that some of them can be released back into the forest.\nOn the last day, we watched a team release two young pangolins into a protected forest. It was an unforgettable moment. Before we left, the director told us that the best way to help wildlife is not to buy any products made from wild animals, and to tell our friends and families to do the same. I will never look at a traditional medicine shop in the same way again.",
    statements: ["The students volunteered at the rescue centre for a week.", "The students' main task was to feed the animals by hand.", "The staff try to keep the animals wild so that some can be released.", "The director said that buying wildlife products is acceptable if they are cheap."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'spent a week volunteering'.\nb) Sai: nhiệm vụ chính là chuẩn bị thức ăn; học sinh 'were not allowed to touch the animals'.\nc) Đúng: 'the staff want them to stay wild so that some of them can be released'.\nd) Sai: giám đốc khuyên không mua bất kì sản phẩm nào từ động vật hoang dã." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nFor decades, wildlife conservation focused mainly on protecting animals inside national parks and nature reserves. Fences were built, rangers patrolled the borders, and local people were often forbidden to enter forests where their families had collected food for generations. While this approach saved some species, it also created conflict. Some villagers, who had lost access to land, began to see wildlife as a problem rather than a treasure.\nToday, many conservationists believe that protecting nature works best when local communities benefit from it. In parts of Africa and Asia, villagers are trained as wildlife guides, earning money from eco-tourists who come to see elephants or rare birds. Others are paid to monitor animal populations or to remove traps from the forest. When people earn a living from living animals, poaching becomes less attractive.\nThis community-based approach is not a magic solution. Tourism can bring pollution and noise, and income is not always shared fairly. Still, many experts agree that conservation without the support of local people is unlikely to succeed in the long term.",
    statements: ["In the past, local people were sometimes forbidden to enter protected forests.", "The old approach to conservation caused no problems with local communities.", "According to the passage, when villagers earn money from living animals, they are less likely to poach.", "The writer believes community-based conservation solves every problem."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'local people were often forbidden to enter forests'.\nb) Sai: 'it also created conflict'.\nc) Đúng: 'When people earn a living from living animals, poaching becomes less attractive'.\nd) Sai: 'This community-based approach is not a magic solution'." },
  { id: 'anh12-8-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-8', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Write a paragraph (120–150 words) about the main causes of wildlife decline and what individuals can do to help protect endangered animals.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn 120–150 từ: 2–3 nguyên nhân (mất môi trường sống, săn bắt trái phép, ô nhiễm/biến đổi khí hậu) và 2–3 hành động cá nhân, câu kết.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: Many wild animals are in danger today for several reasons. The most serious cause is habitat loss. As forests are cut down for farms, roads and cities, animals lose the places where they live and find food. Another cause is illegal hunting. Animals such as rhinos, pangolins and tigers are killed because their body parts are sold at high prices. In addition, pollution and climate change are damaging rivers, oceans and forests. Fortunately, individuals can help. First, we should never buy products made from wild animals, such as ivory or traditional medicines containing animal parts. Second, we can support conservation organisations by donating money or volunteering. Finally, we can raise awareness by sharing reliable information with our friends and family. If everyone acts now, we will be able to protect endangered species for future generations.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Nguyên nhân và giải pháp rõ ràng (4 đ); Bố cục, từ nối (2 đ); Ngữ pháp (2 đ); Từ vựng chủ đề bảo tồn (2 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 9. Career paths =====
  { id: 'anh12-9-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nA ______ school trains students for practical jobs such as electrician, chef or car mechanic.",
    options: ["vocational", "academic", "primary", "boarding"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "vocational school = trường dạy nghề. academic = học thuật; primary = tiểu học; boarding = nội trú." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nMy teacher said that I ______ a good engineer one day.",
    options: ["will become", "would become", "become", "am becoming"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Câu tường thuật với động từ tường thuật ở quá khứ (said) → lùi thì: will → would." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the best response to complete the exchange.\nSon: 'I can't decide whether to study medicine or information technology.'\nCareer adviser: '______'",
    options: ["That's a great idea.", "Congratulations on your success!", "I'm afraid I can't come.", "Why don't you think about which subjects you enjoy and what you're good at?"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Học sinh đang phân vân → người tư vấn đưa ra lời khuyên: 'Why don't you…?'. Các phương án khác không phù hợp." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nBefore choosing a career, ______.",
    options: ["it is choosing carefully", "a job is needed to find", "you should consider your interests, skills and values", "the career will choose you"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Chủ ngữ mệnh đề chính phải là người thực hiện hành động 'choosing' → 'you should consider…'. Các phương án khác sai ngữ pháp hoặc vô nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nJobs in the IT sector often offer good career ______, with many chances to move up to higher positions.",
    options: ["ladder", "promotion", "prospects", "steps"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "career prospects = triển vọng nghề nghiệp (thường dùng với 'good'). 'career ladder' = nấc thang sự nghiệp nhưng không đi với 'offer good'." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence in reported speech, beginning with the given words.\n1. 'I will apply for a scholarship next year,' said Minh.\n→ Minh said ...\n2. 'You should take a gap year to gain some work experience,' my father said to me.\n→ My father advised ...\n3. 'Why did you choose this job?' the interviewer asked her.\n→ The interviewer asked her ...",
    answer: "1. Minh said (that) he would apply for a scholarship the following year / the next year. 2. My father advised me to take a gap year to gain some work experience. 3. The interviewer asked her why she had chosen that job.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. Lùi thì will → would; đổi I → he; next year → the following year.\n2. Lời khuyên: advise sb (not) to V.\n3. Câu hỏi Wh-: asked sb + từ để hỏi + S + V (không đảo ngữ); quá khứ đơn → quá khứ hoàn thành; this → that." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nAfter graduating from medical university, Hoa decided to ______ in her mother's footsteps and became a paediatrician.",
    options: ["go", "walk", "step", "follow"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Thành ngữ 'follow in sb's footsteps' = nối nghiệp, theo bước ai đó." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nThe career adviser suggested ______ a part-time job to gain some experience.",
    options: ["getting", "to get", "get", "got"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "suggest + V-ing (hoặc suggest that + S + (should) V) → getting." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\n'Don't forget to send your application before Friday,' the teacher told us.",
    options: ["The teacher told us not to send our application before Friday.", "The teacher reminded us to send our application before Friday.", "The teacher asked us whether we had sent our application.", "The teacher forgot to send our application before Friday."], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'Don't forget to V' ⇔ remind sb to V (nhắc ai làm gì). A ngược nghĩa; C, D sai nghĩa." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the announcement and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nCAREER FAIR\nNot sure what to do after leaving school? Visit our Career Fair, where more than 40 universities, colleges and companies will be present. You can talk to experts, take a free personality test and (10) ______ advice on writing a CV. Don't miss this chance to plan your future (11) ______ it's too late!",
    options: ["get", "make", "do", "put"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Collocation 'get advice (on sth)' = nhận lời khuyên. Không nói make/do/put advice." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the announcement and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nCAREER FAIR\nNot sure what to do after leaving school? Visit our Career Fair, where more than 40 universities, colleges and companies will be present. You can talk to experts, take a free personality test and (10) ______ advice on writing a CV. Don't miss this chance to plan your future (11) ______ it's too late!",
    options: ["after", "before", "until", "since"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "'before it's too late' = trước khi quá muộn – cụm diễn đạt quen thuộc, hợp nghĩa thúc giục." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nSome students choose to take a gap year between finishing school and starting university. During this year, they may travel, do voluntary work or take a job to save money. Supporters say that a gap year helps young people become more mature and clearer about what they want to study. Critics, however, worry that students may lose their study habits and find it hard to return to education.\nWhich of the following is NOT mentioned as a gap-year activity?",
    options: ["Travelling.", "Doing voluntary work.", "Working to save money.", "Taking university entrance exams."], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Bài nêu 'travel, do voluntary work or take a job to save money'; không nhắc đến thi đầu vào đại học → D." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. I then studied hard to get into a university of architecture.\nb. Now I work for a firm that designs eco-friendly houses.\nc. Ever since I was a child, I have loved drawing buildings.\nd. After graduation, I did an internship at a design company.",
    options: ["c – d – a – b", "a – c – d – b", "c – a – d – b", "c – a – b – d"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Trình tự thời gian: thời thơ ấu (c) → 'then' học đại học kiến trúc (a) → sau tốt nghiệp đi thực tập (d) → hiện tại 'Now' (b)." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nWhen Duy was in Grade 12, everyone expected him to study economics. His parents ran a small business, and they hoped he would one day take it over. Duy, however, had always loved fixing things. As a child, he took apart old radios and fans just to see how they worked.\nAfter many long conversations, his parents agreed to let him attend a two-year vocational course in electrical engineering. Some relatives said it was a waste of his good grades, but Duy was sure of his choice. During the course, he spent most of his time in workshops rather than lecture halls, and he did an internship with a company that installs solar panels.\nToday, at 24, Duy is a team leader at the same company and earns more than many of his friends who went to university. He is also taking evening classes to get a university degree. 'Vocational training was the right start for me,' he says. 'But I never want to stop learning.'",
    statements: ["Duy's parents originally wanted him to study economics.", "All of Duy's relatives supported his decision immediately.", "Duy did an internship with a solar panel company.", "Duy has decided never to study at university."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'everyone expected him to study economics' và bố mẹ mong anh tiếp quản việc kinh doanh.\nb) Sai: 'Some relatives said it was a waste of his good grades'.\nc) Đúng: thực tập ở 'a company that installs solar panels'.\nd) Sai: anh đang học buổi tối để lấy bằng đại học." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nOur grandparents often stayed in the same job, or even with the same employer, for their whole working lives. Today, that pattern is becoming rare. Studies suggest that young people entering the job market now may change careers several times, not just jobs. Rapid technological change is one reason: some professions shrink or disappear, while new ones, such as data analyst or drone pilot, appear almost overnight.\nThis means that choosing a career at eighteen is no longer a final decision. Instead of asking 'What do I want to be?', career experts encourage students to ask 'What problems do I enjoy solving?' and 'What skills can I take with me from one job to another?' Skills such as communication, digital literacy and the ability to learn quickly are valuable in almost every field.\nThat does not mean school-leavers should not plan. A clear first step, whether university, vocational training or work, still matters. But they should see it as the beginning of a path with many turns, rather than a straight road with a single destination.",
    statements: ["According to the passage, people in the past often stayed in one job for a long time.", "The writer suggests that choosing a career at eighteen is a final decision.", "Communication and digital literacy are given as examples of transferable skills.", "The writer advises school-leavers not to make any plans for their future."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: ông bà thường làm cùng một công việc cả đời.\nb) Sai: 'choosing a career at eighteen is no longer a final decision'.\nc) Đúng: đây là những kĩ năng có thể mang từ việc này sang việc khác, 'valuable in almost every field'.\nd) Sai: 'That does not mean school-leavers should not plan. A clear first step… still matters'." },
  { id: 'anh12-9-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-9', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Write a paragraph (120–150 words) about the career you would like to pursue in the future. You should include:\n- what the career is,\n- why you are interested in it,\n- what you need to do to achieve your goal.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn 120–150 từ: nghề nghiệp mơ ước, 2–3 lí do, các bước chuẩn bị (học tập, kĩ năng, kinh nghiệm), câu kết.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: In the future, I would like to become a software engineer. There are several reasons why this career appeals to me. First, I have been interested in computers since I was in secondary school, and I enjoy solving problems step by step. Second, software engineers can create apps that make people's lives easier, which I find very meaningful. Moreover, the IT industry offers good career prospects and the chance to work with people from all over the world. To achieve my goal, I need to study hard, especially maths and English, so that I can get into a good university of technology. I am also planning to take online coding courses and join the school's robotics club to gain practical experience. I believe that with determination and continuous learning, I will be able to make my dream come true.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Đủ 3 ý (4 đ); Bố cục, từ nối (2 đ); Ngữ pháp (2 đ); Từ vựng chủ đề nghề nghiệp (2 đ)." },

  // ===== Unit 10. Lifelong learning =====
  { id: 'anh12-10-01', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\n______ learning means continuing to gain new knowledge and skills throughout your whole life.",
    options: ["Online", "Lifelong", "Formal", "Distance"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "lifelong learning = học tập suốt đời. Online/Distance learning = học trực tuyến/từ xa; Formal learning = học chính quy." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-02', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nIf I had more free time, I ______ a course in photography.",
    options: ["take", "will take", "would take", "would have taken"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Câu điều kiện loại 2 (giả định trái hiện tại): If + quá khứ đơn, S + would + V → would take." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-03', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Speaking & Communication', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the utterances to make a meaningful exchange.\na. I've signed up for an online coding course.\nb. That's great! How do you find the time?\nc. I study for 30 minutes every evening after dinner.",
    options: ["a – b – c", "b – a – c", "a – c – b", "c – b – a"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Thông báo đăng kí khóa học (a) → khen và hỏi lấy thời gian đâu (b) → trả lời cách sắp xếp thời gian (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-04', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nMy grandmother started learning English at the age of 65, ______.",
    options: ["who proves it is too late to learn", "that is too old for learning", "because she was too old to learn", "which proves that it is never too late to learn"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "'which' thay cho cả mệnh đề trước (việc bà học tiếng Anh ở tuổi 65), hợp nghĩa 'không bao giờ là quá muộn để học'. A, C trái nghĩa; B sai ngữ pháp ('that' không đứng sau dấu phẩy)." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-05', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nLearning a new skill can ______ your confidence and open up new opportunities.",
    options: ["rise", "arise", "enlarge", "boost"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "'boost one's confidence' = tăng sự tự tin. rise/arise là nội động từ, không có tân ngữ; enlarge = phóng to (kích thước)." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-06', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'practice', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Rewrite each sentence so that it has the same meaning as the original one, beginning with the given words.\n1. I didn't learn to swim as a child, so I'm afraid of water now.\n→ If I had ...\n2. You won't improve your English unless you practise regularly.\n→ If you ...\n3. It's a pity that I can't speak French.\n→ I wish ...",
    answer: "1. If I had learnt/learned to swim as a child, I wouldn't be afraid of water now. 2. If you don't practise regularly, you won't improve your English. 3. I wish I could speak French.",
    explanation: "Mỗi câu 1 điểm.\n1. Câu điều kiện hỗn hợp: If + quá khứ hoàn thành (trái quá khứ), S + would + V (trái hiện tại).\n2. unless = if … not.\n3. Ước trái hiện tại: I wish + S + could/V2." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-07', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Vocabulary', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nIn a fast-changing job market, workers need to ______ their skills regularly to stay competitive.",
    options: ["brush up on", "put off", "give up", "take after"], answer: 0,
    explanation: "brush up on = ôn luyện, trau dồi lại. put off = trì hoãn; give up = từ bỏ; take after = giống (người thân)." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-08', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the option that best completes the sentence.\nIf she ______ the online marketing course last year, she would have a better job now.",
    options: ["took", "had taken", "has taken", "would take"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Câu điều kiện hỗn hợp: giả định trái quá khứ (last year) → If + quá khứ hoàn thành; kết quả trái hiện tại (now) → would + V." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-09', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Grammar', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the sentence that is closest in meaning to the given one.\nHe stopped learning after university, so he can't keep up with new technology now.",
    options: ["If he didn't stop learning after university, he can keep up with new technology now.", "If he hadn't stopped learning after university, he couldn't keep up with new technology now.", "If he hadn't stopped learning after university, he could keep up with new technology now.", "Unless he had stopped learning after university, he couldn't keep up with new technology now."], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Điều kiện trái quá khứ (đã ngừng học) → If + had not + V3; kết quả trái hiện tại (bây giờ không theo kịp) → could + V (khẳng định). B, D sai nghĩa; A sai cấu trúc." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-10', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'NB', difficulty: 1, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the notice and choose the option that best fits blank (10).\nCOMMUNITY LEARNING CENTRE – EVENING CLASSES\nIt's never too late to learn something new! This autumn we offer courses in cooking, basic computing, foreign languages and first aid. Classes are held twice a week and are open to adults of all ages. (10) ______ you are a busy parent or a retired teacher, there is a course for you. Fees are low, and learners over 60 can study (11) ______ charge.",
    options: ["If", "Whether", "Unless", "Although"], answer: 1,
    explanation: "Cấu trúc 'Whether … or …' = dù là … hay … → 'Whether you are a busy parent or a retired teacher'." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-11', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the notice and choose the option that best fits blank (11).\nCOMMUNITY LEARNING CENTRE – EVENING CLASSES\nIt's never too late to learn something new! This autumn we offer courses in cooking, basic computing, foreign languages and first aid. Classes are held twice a week and are open to adults of all ages. (10) ______ you are a busy parent or a retired teacher, there is a course for you. Fees are low, and learners over 60 can study (11) ______ charge.",
    options: ["for", "out of", "free of", "by"], answer: 2,
    explanation: "Cụm cố định 'free of charge' = miễn phí." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-12', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and answer the question.\nMassive Open Online Courses, or MOOCs, allow anyone with an Internet connection to study subjects taught by university professors. Many courses are free, although learners may pay a small fee for a certificate. MOOCs are especially popular among working adults, who can study at their own pace. However, only a small percentage of people who sign up actually finish their courses, mainly because they lack motivation without a teacher checking on them.\nAccording to the passage, why do many learners not finish MOOCs?",
    options: ["They lack motivation without a teacher checking on them.", "The courses are too expensive.", "They do not have an Internet connection.", "The certificates are not useful."], answer: 0,
    explanation: "Câu cuối: 'mainly because they lack motivation without a teacher checking on them'. B trái với 'Many courses are free'." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-13', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Reading', type: 'mcq', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Choose the correct arrangement of the sentences to make a meaningful paragraph.\na. In addition, it keeps the brain active and may slow down memory loss in old age.\nb. Lifelong learning brings many benefits to individuals.\nc. In short, learning should not stop when we leave school.\nd. First, it helps people adapt to changes in their jobs.",
    options: ["b – a – d – c", "d – b – a – c", "b – d – c – a", "b – d – a – c"], answer: 3,
    explanation: "Câu chủ đề (b) → First (d) → In addition (a) → kết luận 'In short' (c)." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-14', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'TH', difficulty: 2, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nMrs Hanh retired from her job as a bank clerk at the age of 60. For the first few months, she enjoyed resting, but soon she began to feel bored and lonely. Her granddaughter suggested that she join a free smartphone class for older people at the local library.\nAt first, Mrs Hanh was nervous. She had never used a touch screen, and she was afraid of pressing the wrong button. The teacher, a university student, was very patient and explained everything slowly. After eight weeks, Mrs Hanh could send messages, make video calls and read the news online.\nThe class changed her life. She now video-calls her son, who works in Germany, every Sunday. She has also joined an online group for people who love gardening, where she shares photos of her orchids. Encouraged by her success, she has signed up for an English course. 'My brain feels younger,' she says with a smile. 'I wish I had started learning new things earlier.'",
    statements: ["Mrs Hanh worked as a teacher before she retired.", "Her granddaughter suggested the smartphone class.", "The smartphone class lasted for eight weeks.", "Mrs Hanh has decided not to learn anything else after the smartphone class."],
    answer: [false, true, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Sai: bà là nhân viên ngân hàng (bank clerk).\nb) Đúng: 'Her granddaughter suggested that she join a free smartphone class'.\nc) Đúng: 'After eight weeks, Mrs Hanh could…'.\nd) Sai: bà đã đăng kí học tiếng Anh." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-15', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Reading', type: 'tf', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Read the passage and decide whether each statement is True or False.\nIt is often said that learning becomes much harder as we get older. While it is true that children pick up some skills, such as the accent of a new language, more easily, research shows that adults have important advantages too. Adults usually have more background knowledge, which helps them connect new information to what they already know. They also tend to be better at organising their time and setting clear goals.\nWhat often stops adults from learning is not their brain but their circumstances. Work, family responsibilities and a lack of confidence can make it difficult to start. Many adults also remember negative experiences from school and fear being judged if they make mistakes.\nTo overcome these barriers, experts recommend starting small. Learning for just fifteen minutes a day is more effective than studying for three hours once a month. Choosing a subject that is personally meaningful, such as a language needed for travel or a skill useful at work, also increases motivation. Finally, learning with others, whether in a class or an online community, can provide valuable support and encouragement.",
    statements: ["According to the passage, children generally learn the accent of a new language more easily than adults.", "Adults have no advantages over children when it comes to learning.", "The writer suggests that circumstances, rather than the brain, often prevent adults from learning.", "Experts recommend studying for long periods once a month instead of a little every day."],
    answer: [true, false, true, false],
    explanation: "a) Đúng: 'children pick up some skills, such as the accent of a new language, more easily'.\nb) Sai: 'adults have important advantages too' (kiến thức nền, kĩ năng tổ chức thời gian).\nc) Đúng: 'What often stops adults from learning is not their brain but their circumstances'.\nd) Sai: học 15 phút mỗi ngày hiệu quả hơn học 3 giờ mỗi tháng một lần." },
  { id: 'anh12-10-16', subject: 'anh', grade: 12, chapter: 'anh12-10', topic: 'Writing', type: 'essay', level: 'VD', difficulty: 3, pool: 'exam', source: 'Tự biên soạn',
    content: "Some people think that learning should stop when they finish school or university. Do you agree or disagree? Write a paragraph (120–150 words) to express your opinion about the importance of lifelong learning.",
    answer: "Đoạn văn nghị luận 120–150 từ: nêu rõ quan điểm (không đồng ý), 2–3 lí do kèm ví dụ, câu kết.",
    explanation: "Bài mẫu tham khảo: I strongly disagree with the idea that learning should stop after we leave school or university. Firstly, the world is changing very quickly, especially because of technology. Skills that were useful ten years ago may be out of date today, so workers have to keep learning to keep their jobs and get promoted. Secondly, lifelong learning is good for our health. Studies suggest that learning new things, such as a foreign language or a musical instrument, keeps the brain active and may slow down memory loss in old age. Finally, learning brings personal satisfaction. My grandfather started painting when he retired, and he says it has made him happier than ever. In conclusion, education should be seen as a lifelong journey rather than something that ends with a diploma.\nTiêu chí chấm (10 điểm): Quan điểm rõ ràng (1 đ); Lập luận, ví dụ thuyết phục (4 đ); Bố cục, từ nối (2 đ); Ngữ pháp, có thể dùng câu điều kiện (2 đ); Từ vựng chủ đề (1 đ)." }
);
